WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:06.499
The next morning Swallow was eager to catch up to the flock.

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.041
He flew up to say good-bye to the statue.

3
00:00:11.042 --> 00:00:14.749
"Thank you for keeping me warm last night," he said.

4
00:00:14.750 --> 00:00:20.666
The statue sighed. "You're welcome.

5
00:00:20.667 --> 00:00:25.365
Thank you for listening to my sad story."

6
00:00:25.366 --> 00:00:30.082
"I hope you find a way to be happy," Swallow said.

7
00:00:30.083 --> 00:00:36.291
"I won't—not until everyone has what he or she needs."

8
00:00:36.292 --> 00:00:41.082
Swallow never had to think about what anyone else needed.

9
00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:44.004
The flock leader did that.

10
00:00:44.005 --> 00:00:48.416
Leader looked after all the birds.

11
00:00:48.417 --> 00:00:53.332
"Too bad there's nothing you can do," Swallow said.

12
00:00:53.333 --> 00:01:01.166
"There are things that I could do," the statue said. "If only I could move."

13
00:01:01.167 --> 00:01:04.875
Perhaps the swallow should have left then.

14
00:01:04.876 --> 00:01:09.374
But he had been thinking about the statue's unhappiness.

15
00:01:09.375 --> 00:01:13.782
He had been thinking about the townspeople's misery too.

16
00:01:13.783 --> 00:01:17.874
"Tell me your idea, Prince."

17
00:01:17.875 --> 00:01:27.582
Swallow listened carefully. "You're sure you want to do this?"

18
00:01:27.583 --> 00:01:30.374
"Absolutely!"

19
00:01:30.375 --> 00:01:34.303
"Okay," Swallow said.

20
00:01:34.304 --> 00:01:38.874
"First, I'll do what you asked. Then I'll leave for Egypt.

21
00:01:38.875 --> 00:01:41.969
I hope this will make you happier."

22
00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:46.207
"Thank you, Swallow."

23
00:01:46.208 --> 00:01:50.766
Swallow flew down to the statue's belt.

24
00:01:50.767 --> 00:01:55.749
He gripped one of the rubies with his beak and pulled.

25
00:01:55.750 --> 00:02:00.416
Then he flew off, carrying the jewel. ***

26
00:02:00.417 --> 00:02:03.644
Swallow flew to the edge of town.

27
00:02:03.645 --> 00:02:08.999
He soon spotted where the statue had told him to go.

28
00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.478
It was a one-room house.

29
00:02:12.479 --> 00:02:15.457
He looked inside.

30
00:02:15.458 --> 00:02:20.169
The room was empty except for a table and bed.

31
00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:23.624
A woman sat at the table sewing a dress.

32
00:02:23.625 --> 00:02:26.679
But this wasn't just any dress.

33
00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:33.166
It was a beautiful ballgown covered in shiny crystals.

34
00:02:33.167 --> 00:02:37.740
Swallow gasped. "That's stunning!

35
00:02:37.741 --> 00:02:41.207
She doesn't need this jewel.

36
00:02:41.208 --> 00:02:44.788
I'll return it to the statue and then leave for Egypt!"

37
00:02:44.789 --> 00:02:47.933
Swallow hopped to the edge of the windowsill.

38
00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:54.624
He was about to take flight when someone began coughing.

39
00:02:54.625 --> 00:02:57.633
Swallow looked closer.

40
00:02:57.634 --> 00:03:02.923
It was a little boy. He looked very sick.

41
00:03:02.924 --> 00:03:06.798
"My poor baby," the woman said.

42
00:03:06.799 --> 00:03:10.541
"We will have money for medicine soon.

43
00:03:10.542 --> 00:03:16.374
As soon as I finish this ballgown for a lady."

44
00:03:16.375 --> 00:03:20.633
"Oh!" Swallow realized.

45
00:03:20.634 --> 00:03:24.457
"The seamstress is making the dress for someone else.

46
00:03:24.458 --> 00:03:28.863
She really does need this jewel."

47
00:03:28.864 --> 00:03:35.559
Whoosh! Swallow zoomed inside and dropped the jewel in the woman's lap.

48
00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:39.541
Then he flew out the window before she could see him.

49
00:03:39.542 --> 00:03:46.999
The woman gasped. "A gift from above!

50
00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:58.109
It seems impossible. But now I can buy my boy his medicine!"

